@startuml Teaching

!include style.puml

title From logical gates to the ion chain

left to right direction

rectangle "Logical circuit\n(h, cx, rz, ...)" as logical
rectangle "Native gate sequence\nGPI, GPI2, MS or ZZ, VirtualZ" as native
rectangle "Bloch sphere per ion\n(one native gate at a time)" as bloch

logical -right-> native : transpile + translate
native -right-> bloch : simulate + vectorize

note bottom of native
  This is the gap that the visualiser opens:
  the abstract circuit and what the machine
  really runs are not the same thing.
end note

note bottom of bloch
  Every native gate can be watched,
  so the physics behind it can be explained.
end note

@enduml
